1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,300
Children do not ask to be born, and each deserves an opportunity to thrive.

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:16,300
I would argue that caring and concerned adults, that includes you, have an obligation to support the learning and development of all children, heavy on all, underscore, bold, italicized.

3
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:29,780
If you do nothing else this Pride Month, identify ways that you, yes, you, can recognize, respect, and protect the rights of all young people, especially those most likely to be targeted, tormented, and terrorized.

4
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,800
Consider the following three things as you build your capacity toolbox.

5
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:35,780
First, words matter.

6
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:38,700
Ask the young people around you how they want to be respected.

7
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:42,400
Beyond pronouns which are important to respect, ask the following.

8
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,380
How do you want me to acknowledge you today?

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,760
How do you want me to acknowledge you in front of your peers?

10
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:51,080
And if you aren't their parents, ask, how do you want me to acknowledge you in front of your parents?

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,620
Two, protect peace.

12
00:00:53,620 --> 00:01:03,420
While we can't mandate or legislate tolerance or acceptance, we can pass policies and inform practices prohibiting discrimination and promoting inclusive communities.

13
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:17,220
Title IX is the federal law designed to prevent discrimination on the basis of sex, and codification of the Equality Act will make explicit protections on the basis of sexual identity or sexual orientation, gender identity, and expression.

14
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:26,580
You should call your representatives at 202-224-3121 and urge support for the Equality Act today.

15
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:33,000
And then three, take a cue from Aunt Aretha who underscores the importance of respect.

16
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:38,060
Do something to support the young people you know in making sense of the world around them.

17
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:41,320
Look up the history of drag and trace it through time and space.

18
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:50,860
Learn about the life and legacy of Black queer superheroes like Marsha Payin' No Mind Johnson, Brother Bayard Rustin, Malcolm Kenyatta, and Angelica Ross.

19
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:53,980
Visit MBJC's Been Here Digital Archive for more.

20
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:55,480
And ask for help.

21
00:01:55,820 --> 00:02:00,260
You're not supposed to know everything, and you should find comfort in disabusing yourself of that fallacy.

22
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,340
You cannot know everything.

23
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,440
Ask for help.

24
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:10,700
There are hundreds of us living and laboring and loving so that you can find strategies to advocate and exist as a safe space for others.

25
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:14,020
Whatever you do, do something to support the babies.

26
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:14,840
Happy Pride.

